        </div>
        <div class="px-6 py-5 prose-dark">
          <p class="text-silver-400 text-sm leading-relaxed"><strong>Information You Provide Voluntarily:</strong> If you contact us via our <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> or email, we collect the information you submit such as your name and email address. We do not require user registration to use any of our tools.</p>
          <p class="text-silver-400 text-sm leading-relaxed"><strong>VIN Data:</strong> When you use our VIN decoder or recall checker, the VIN you enter is sent directly to the NHTSA API from your browser. We do not store, log, or retain the VINs you look up on our servers.</p>
          <p class="text-silver-400 text-sm leading-relaxed"><strong>VIN Scanner:</strong> Our camera-based VIN scanner runs entirely in your browser using client-side OCR. No images, video frames, or camera data are transmitted to our servers or any third party.</p>
          <p class="text-silver-400 text-sm leading-relaxed"><strong>Automatically Collected Data:</strong> Like most websites, we collect standard technical information through server logs and analytics tools, including IP addresses, browser type, operating system, referring URLs, pages visited, and timestamps. This data is used in aggregate for site performance analysis and is not linked to individual identities.</p>
        </div>
